%S A402110 1,2,6,7,48,55,705,861,21454,26696,1311647,1650868,159700301,
%T A402110 203876423,38793597533,50267162348,18813432952718,24740950757971,
%U A402110 18214241752384042,24308866374664609,35202421967310524907,47679458745513208679,135816297628039732398886
%N A402110 Number of n X n binary arrays invariant under all rotations and reflections of the square in which every 1 has another 1 as a horizontal, vertical or diagonal neighbor.
%C A402110 Equivalently, the number of vertex subsets of the n X n king graph invariant under all eight symmetries of the square whose induced subgraphs have no isolated vertices. The empty subset is included.
%C A402110 These arrays arise in James Guillochon's study of Vinciolo's lace patterns.
%H A402110 James Guillochon, <a href="/A402110/b402110.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..47</a>
%H A402110 James Guillochon, <a href="https://groups.google.com/g/seqfan/c/4hbZq_2eAhQ/m/KsB6u220AQAJ">A new sequence: Vinciolo's Lace</a>, SeqFan, Nov 09 2026.
%H A402110 James Guillochon, <a href="https://guillochon.github.io/vinciolo-lace/">Vinciolo's Lace</a>.
%H A402110 James Guillochon, <a href="https://github.com/guillochon/oeis-results/tree/main/vinciolo-lace">Symmetric lace designs without pinholes, and the minimum-region table</a>.
%H A402110 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KingGraph.html">King Graph</a>.
%e A402110 For n = 3, the corner cells, edge-center cells and central cell form three symmetry orbits. Of their eight unions, only the central cell alone and the four corners alone contain isolated selected cells, so a(3) = 6.
%t A402110 a[n_] := Module[{o, b}, o = GatherBy[Tuples[Range[n], 2], Sort[Abs[2 # - n - 1]] &]; b = Table[Boole[AnyTrue[o[[j]], Max[Abs[o[[i, 1]] - #]] == 1 &]], {i, Length[o]}, {j, Length[o]}]; Count[Tuples[{0, 1}, Length[o]], s_ /; And @@ Thread[b.s >= s]]]; Array[a, 10]
%Y A402110 Cf. A202788 (arrays without the symmetry restriction).
%K A402110 nonn,more,new
%O A402110 1,2
%A A402110 _Eric W. Weisstein_, Nov 13 2026
